/-!
# Local generation by `r` sections of `𝓕ᵃ` on the small étale site

Descent, Lemma 05VG asserts, for each property of modules of Modules on Sites, Definitions
03DE, 03DL and 03ER, that a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓕` has the property if and only if
`𝓕ᵃ` has it as an `𝒪`-module on the site.  **This file lands the bounded local-generation
clause, Definition 03DL (4), at the small étale site**, as an equivalence, under the source's
hypothesis that `𝓕` be quasi-coherent and nothing else.

The unbounded clause 03DL (3) is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_associatedModule_iff`, and it
is settled by proving both of its sides outright from quasi-coherence: quasi-coherent data
supplies, on a covering of the final object, a presentation whose generators are generating
sections.  That argument says nothing here, because it produces whatever index type the
presentation happens to have and the bounded clause fixes the index type to `Fin r`.  So this
file runs the source's own route, the covering argument of Stacks 03DN together with a descent
lemma for the property itself, which is the route the other local clauses at this site take.

## The two halves

* The `only if` half is the covering argument at the small Zariski site.  Stacks 03DN there,
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_exists_cover_generators`, produces a
  Zariski covering of `S` on whose members `𝓕` is generated by `r` sections; the image of that
  covering under `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.opensToSmallEtale` covers the final object of
  `S_étale`, and on a member the restriction of `𝓕ᵃ` is again generated by `r` sections by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_associatedModuleOver`.
  Stacks 03DN at `S_étale` assembles the conclusion.  No quasi-coherence enters this half.
* The `if` half is the descent.  Stacks 03DN at `S_étale` produces a family covering the final
  object on whose members `𝓕ᵃ` is generated by `r` sections; the members are étale over `S`,
  hence flat, locally of finite presentation and jointly surjective, so their structure
  morphisms are an fpqc covering family of `S` on the nose
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.presieve₀_mem_fpqcPrecoverage_coveringHypercover`).  On a
  member the crossover of Stacks 06WI and Stacks 03DV at an object rewrite the restriction of
  `𝓕ᵃ` as `(f^*𝓕)ᵃ` on the small étale site of the scheme of the member, where 05VG for Modules
  on Sites 03DE (4) — `…isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff_associatedModule`, an `iff` —
  reflects the verdict down to `f^*𝓕`, which is quasi-coherent by Stacks 01BG.  Stacks 082U,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isCardinalGenerated_of_pullback_fpqc`, then descends the bound to `S`.

## The descent input

Stacks 082U is stated for `SheafOfModules.IsCardinalGenerated` with bound the cardinal of `r`,
that is for local generating families of *at most* `r` sections, while Definition 03DL (4) asks
for families indexed by a type equivalent to `Fin r`.  The two agree, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_of_isCardinalGenerated` is the comparison: a
family of at most `r` sections is padded out to one of exactly `r` by the zero section, which
changes neither the span nor the covering.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_of_isCardinalGenerated`: a cardinal bound of `r`
  on the local generators of a module on a scheme is local generation by `r` sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_associatedModuleOver`:
  generation by `r` sections of `𝓕|_V` over an open `V` of `S` is generation by `r` sections of
  `(𝓕ᵃ)|_{V_étale}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_pullback_of_over`: generation
  by `r` sections of `(𝓕ᵃ)|_{S_étale/U}` is generation by `r` sections of `f^*𝓕`, for `f` the
  structure morphism of an object `U` of `S_étale`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_associatedModule_iff`:
  **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (4), at the small étale site.**

